# Git Interview Questions and Answers – Part 1

This covers some of the most commonly asked basic Git interview questions along with clear and concise answers. These questions are useful for beginners as well as professionals preparing for DevOps, Developer, or SCM-related interviews.

---

## 1. Is Git a Distributed or Centralized Version Control System? What is the Difference?

Git is a **Distributed Version Control System (DVCS)**.

### Centralized Version Control System (CVCS)
Examples: SVN, CVS  
- Uses a client-server architecture.
- All versions of the code are stored in a central server.
- Developers depend on the server for history and versions.

### Distributed Version Control System (DVCS)
Example: Git  
- Every developer has a complete copy of the repository.
- All versions and history are stored locally.
- No dependency on a central server for accessing history.

The main difference is that in DVCS, the entire repository history is distributed to every developer.

